==English==

===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|nrf|croquet|t=hook}}, from {{der|en|ONF.|croquet}}. {{doublet|en|crochet|crocket|crotchet}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{enPR|krō'kā}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈkɹəʊkeɪ/|/ˈkɹəʊki/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-croquet.wav |Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|krōkā'}}, {{IPA|en|/kɹoʊˈkeɪ/}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable|games}} A [[game]] played on a [[lawn]], in which players use [[mallet]]s to drive [[ball]]s through [[hoop]]s ([[wicket]]s).
# {{lb|en|countable|games}} A [[shot]] in this game in which the striker's ball and another ball are moved by hitting the striker's ball when they have been placed in contact following a [[roquet]].
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[croquette]].

